  "causal_attribution": {
    "observation": "CPU-to-Chip writes submitted before abort were not complete when cutpoint 4 entered its memory-driven hold. They became visible during the physical Freezer interval.",
    "mechanism": [
      "c2_stream_c2d_write returns success immediately after the DMA trigger and carries no content-completion proof.",
      "c2_append_stage_copy_phase writes Bank 2 from readback and then reads Bank 2 back into that same already-correct buffer; an uncompleted read can therefore leave expected bytes in place and falsely satisfy the comparison.",
      "rollback unpublish/finalize can restore header and clear C2J while late Bank-2 and export-journal writes remain able to land afterward."
    ],
    "scope": "This is the previously unproved CPU-to-Chip write direction. It does not contradict the accepted Chip-Bank-to-window read prefilter; it exposes a different transport seam."
  },
